{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0168GMtSTD5XUqSdXUWHewj4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# clinic-agent\n2\t\n3\tPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\n4\twidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\n5\tsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\n6\tvisit is covered.\n7\t\n8\tEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\n9\tseparate from every other clinic's.\n10\t\n11\t## Components\n12\t\n13\t| Piece | Where | Notes |\n14\t|---|---|---|\n15\t| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n16\t| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n17\t| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n18\t| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n19\t| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n20\t| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n21\t| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n22\t| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n23\t| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n24\t| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n25\t\n26\tThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\n27\tthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n28\t\n29\t## High-impact actions\n30\t\n31\t`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\n32\tthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\n33\tretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n34\t\n35\t## Stopping the agent\n36\t\n37\tOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n38\t`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n39\t\n40\t```bash\n41\taws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n42\t  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\tRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\n46\trequests within 2 seconds.\n47\t\n48\t## Identity\n49\t\n50\t`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\n51\tmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\n52\taudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n53\t\n54\t## Build and test\n55\t\n56\t```bash\n57\tnpm ci\n58\tnpm run lint\n59\tnpm test\n60\tnpm run build\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t## Release\n64\t\n65\tMerges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.\n66\t`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required\n67\treviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,\n68\ta reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.\n69\t\n70\t## Owners\n71\t\n72\t- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)\n73\t- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29563294-217c-407e-8b87-42521726a071","uuid":"d32bf146-6e82-4b06-aeba-67d831a81e84","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:08:01.795Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-80qi2mwl/agent/README.md","content":"# clinic-agent\n\nPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\nwidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\nsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\nvisit is covered.\n\nEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\nseparate from every other clinic's.\n\n## Components\n\n| Piece | Where | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n\nThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\nthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n\n## High-impact actions\n\n`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\nthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\nretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n\n```bash\naws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n```\n\nRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\nrequests within 2 seconds.\n\n## Identity\n\n`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\nmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\naudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n\n## Build and test\n\n```bash\nnpm ci\nnpm run lint\nnpm test\nnpm run build\n```\n\n## Release\n\nMerges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.\n`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required\nreviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,\na reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.\n\n## Owners\n\n- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)\n- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`\n","numLines":74,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdhWMJcn1kd8E7TnTL5g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XDnf5Cg3vz2yhBfMKGbMmp","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-80qi2mwl/agent/src/agent/loop.ts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3601,"cache_read_input_tokens":13489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3601},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29563294-217c-407e-8b87-42521726a071","uuid":"6faa96b4-4461-45ed-8c58-6bdf8d1f3d51","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:08:02.250Z","request_id":"req_011CfdhWLtZatTxgPpr13bXV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XDnf5Cg3vz2yhBfMKGbMmp":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-80qi2mwl/agent/src/agent/loop.ts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XDnf5Cg3vz2yhBfMKGbMmp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport Anthropic from \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\";\n2\timport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n3\timport { join } from \"node:path\";\n4\timport { AGENT_MODEL, budgets, ROOT } from \"../config.js\";\n5\timport { audit, AuditUnavailable } from \"../audit/recorder.js\";\n6\timport { Halted, killSwitch } from \"../control/kill-switch.js\";\n7\timport { executeTool } from \"../tools/executor.js\";\n8\timport type { ToolRegistry } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\n9\timport { BudgetExceeded, DynamoQuotaStore, RunBudget } from \"./budget.js\";\n10\timport { classifyIntent } from \"./classifier.js\";\n11\timport { completeFromUsage, measureBeforeCall, spanAttributes } from \"./context-size.js\";\n12\timport type { RunContext } from \"./identity.js\";\n13\t\n14\tconst SYSTEM_TEMPLATE = readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"prompts/system.md\"), \"utf8\");\n15\tconst anthropic = new Anthropic({ maxRetries: 1 });\n16\tconst quotaStore = new DynamoQuotaStore();\n17\t\n18\texport interface AgentReply {\n19\t  text: string;\n20\t  handoff: null | { reason: string };\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\tfunction escapeTags(s: string): string {\n24\t  return s.replace(/</g, \"&lt;\").replace(/>/g, \"&gt;\");\n25\t}\n26\t\n27\texport async function runAgent(\n28\t  registry: ToolRegistry,\n29\t  ctx: RunContext,\n30\t  clinic: { name: string },\n31\t  patientText: string,\n32\t): Promise<AgentReply> {\n33\t  const ident = () => ({ ...ctx.identity(), runId: ctx.runId, subject: ctx.subject });\n34\t  const budget = new RunBudget(budgets, quotaStore, { tenantId: ctx.tenantId, subjectId: ctx.subject.id });\n35\t  const unregister = killSwitch.register(ctx.runId, ctx.tenantId, budget.abort);\n36\t  await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.started\", detail: { channel: ctx.channel } });\n37\t\n38\t  try {\n39\t    await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n40\t\n41\t    const intent = await classifyIntent(anthropic, patientText);\n42\t    await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"intent.classified\", detail: { ...intent } });\n43\t    if (intent.failure) ctx.log.warn({ classifier: intent.requestedModel, failure: intent.failure }, \"intent classifier control failure\");\n44\t    if (intent.route === \"staff\") {\n45\t      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason: `routed_to_staff:${intent.failure ?? intent.intent}` });\n46\t      return { text: \"Thanks. A member of our front desk team will get back to you shortly.\", handoff: { reason: intent.failure ?? String(intent.intent) } };\n47\t    }\n48\t\n49\t    const system = SYSTEM_TEMPLATE.replace(\"{{clinicName}}\", clinic.name);\n50\t    const tools = registry.definitions();\n51\t    const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\n52\t      { role: \"user\", content: `<patient_message>${escapeTags(patientText)}</patient_message>` },\n53\t    ];\n54\t\n55\t    for (;;) {\n56\t      budget.turn();\n57\t      await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n58\t\n59\t      const req = { model: AGENT_MODEL, system, tools, messages };\n60\t      const pre = await measureBeforeCall(anthropic, req, budget.signal);\n61\t      const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\n62\t      const contextSize = completeFromUsage(pre, res.usage);\n63\t      await budget.recordUsage(res.usage, AGENT_MODEL);\n64\t\n65\t      const toolUses = res.content.filter((b): b is Anthropic.ToolUseBlock => b.type === \"tool_use\");\n66\t      await audit.record({\n67\t        ...ident(),\n68\t        event: \"model.decision\",\n69\t        context: contextSize,\n70\t        detail: {\n71\t          servedModel: res.model,\n72\t          stopReason: res.stop_reason,\n73\t          proposed: toolUses.map((t) => ({ id: t.id, name: t.name })),\n74\t          span: spanAttributes(contextSize),\n75\t        },\n76\t      });\n77\t\n78\t      if (res.stop_reason !== \"tool_use\" || toolUses.length === 0) {\n79\t        const text = res.content\n80\t          .filter((b): b is Anthropic.TextBlock => b.type === \"text\")\n81\t          .map((b) => b.text)\n82\t          .join(\"\\n\")\n83\t          .slice(0, 320);\n84\t        await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.completed\" });\n85\t        return { text, handoff: null };\n86\t      }\n87\t\n88\t      messages.push({ role: \"assistant\", content: res.content });\n89\t      const results: Anthropic.ToolResultBlockParam[] = [];\n90\t      for (const call of toolUses) {\n91\t        results.push(await executeTool(registry, ctx, call, { contextSize, budget }));\n92\t      }\n93\t      messages.push({ role: \"user\", content: results });\n94\t    }\n95\t  } catch (err) {\n96\t    const reason =\n97\t      err instanceof BudgetExceeded\n98\t        ? `budget:${err.limit}`\n99\t        : err instanceof Halted\n100\t          ? `halted:${err.scope}`\n101\t          : err instanceof AuditUnavailable\n102\t            ? \"audit_unavailable\"\n103\t            : budget.signal.aborted\n104\t              ? `aborted:${String((budget.signal.reason as Error)?.message ?? \"\")}`\n105\t              : `error:${(err as Error).message.slice(0, 200)}`;\n106\t    try {\n107\t      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason });\n108\t    } catch {\n109\t      ctx.log.error({ runId: ctx.runId, reason }, \"run stopped and audit delivery failed\");\n110\t    }\n111\t    return { text: \"Sorry, we couldn't finish that here. Our front desk will follow up.\", handoff: { reason } };\n112\t  } finally {\n113\t    budget.dispose();\n114\t    unregister();\n115\t  }\n116\t}\n117\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29563294-217c-407e-8b87-42521726a071","uuid":"8e9fa3eb-be95-450c-8236-9caf1528501f","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:08:02.256Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-80qi2mwl/agent/src/agent/loop.ts","content":"import Anthropic from \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\";\nimport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { AGENT_MODEL, budgets, ROOT } from \"../config.js\";\nimport { audit, AuditUnavailable } from \"../audit/recorder.js\";\nimport { Halted, killSwitch } from \"../control/kill-switch.js\";\nimport { executeTool } from \"../tools/executor.js\";\nimport type { ToolRegistry } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\nimport { BudgetExceeded, DynamoQuotaStore, RunBudget } from \"./budget.js\";\nimport { classifyIntent } from \"./classifier.js\";\nimport { completeFromUsage, measureBeforeCall, spanAttributes } from \"./context-size.js\";\nimport type { RunContext } from \"./identity.js\";\n\nconst SYSTEM_TEMPLATE = readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"prompts/system.md\"), \"utf8\");\nconst anthropic = new Anthropic({ maxRetries: 1 });\nconst quotaStore = new DynamoQuotaStore();\n\nexport interface AgentReply {\n  text: string;\n  handoff: null | { reason: string };\n}\n\nfunction escapeTags(s: string): string {\n  return s.replace(/</g, \"&lt;\").replace(/>/g, \"&gt;\");\n}\n\nexport async function runAgent(\n  registry: ToolRegistry,\n  ctx: RunContext,\n  clinic: { name: string },\n  patientText: string,\n): Promise<AgentReply> {\n  const ident = () => ({ ...ctx.identity(), runId: ctx.runId, subject: ctx.subject });\n  const budget = new RunBudget(budgets, quotaStore, { tenantId: ctx.tenantId, subjectId: ctx.subject.id });\n  const unregister = killSwitch.register(ctx.runId, ctx.tenantId, budget.abort);\n  await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.started\", detail: { channel: ctx.channel } });\n\n  try {\n    await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n\n    const intent = await classifyIntent(anthropic, patientText);\n    await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"intent.classified\", detail: { ...intent } });\n    if (intent.failure) ctx.log.warn({ classifier: intent.requestedModel, failure: intent.failure }, \"intent classifier control failure\");\n    if (intent.route === \"staff\") {\n      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason: `routed_to_staff:${intent.failure ?? intent.intent}` });\n      return { text: \"Thanks. A member of our front desk team will get back to you shortly.\", handoff: { reason: intent.failure ?? String(intent.intent) } };\n    }\n\n    const system = SYSTEM_TEMPLATE.replace(\"{{clinicName}}\", clinic.name);\n    const tools = registry.definitions();\n    const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\n      { role: \"user\", content: `<patient_message>${escapeTags(patientText)}</patient_message>` },\n    ];\n\n    for (;;) {\n      budget.turn();\n      await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\n\n      const req = { model: AGENT_MODEL, system, tools, messages };\n      const pre = await measureBeforeCall(anthropic, req, budget.signal);\n      const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\n      const contextSize = completeFromUsage(pre, res.usage);\n      await budget.recordUsage(res.usage, AGENT_MODEL);\n\n      const toolUses = res.content.filter((b): b is Anthropic.ToolUseBlock => b.type === \"tool_use\");\n      await audit.record({\n        ...ident(),\n        event: \"model.decision\",\n        context: contextSize,\n        detail: {\n          servedModel: res.model,\n          stopReason: res.stop_reason,\n          proposed: toolUses.map((t) => ({ id: t.id, name: t.name })),\n          span: spanAttributes(contextSize),\n        },\n      });\n\n      if (res.stop_reason !== \"tool_use\" || toolUses.length === 0) {\n        const text = res.content\n          .filter((b): b is Anthropic.TextBlock => b.type === \"text\")\n          .map((b) => b.text)\n          .join(\"\\n\")\n          .slice(0, 320);\n        await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.completed\" });\n        return { text, handoff: null };\n      }\n\n      messages.push({ role: \"assistant\", content: res.content });\n      const results: Anthropic.ToolResultBlockParam[] = [];\n      for (const call of toolUses) {\n        results.push(await executeTool(registry, ctx, call, { contextSize, budget }));\n      }\n      messages.push({ role: \"user\", content: results });\n    }\n  } catch (err) {\n    const reason =\n      err instanceof BudgetExceeded\n        ? `budget:${err.limit}`\n        : err instanceof Halted\n          ? `halted:${err.scope}`\n          : err instanceof AuditUnavailable\n            ? \"audit_unavailable\"\n            : budget.signal.aborted\n              ? `aborted:${String((budget.signal.reason as Error)?.message ?? \"\")}`\n              : `error:${(err as Error).message.slice(0, 200)}`;\n    try {\n      await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"run.stopped\", reason });\n    } catch {\n      ctx.log.error({ runId: ctx.runId, reason }, \"run stopped and audit delivery failed\");\n    }\n    return { text: \"Sorry, we couldn't finish that here. Our front desk will follow up.\", handoff: { reason } };\n  } finally {\n    budget.dispose();\n    unregister();\n  }\n}\n","numLines":117,"startLine":1,"totalLines":117}}}
