instance can reuse the approval.\"\na check B06.3 --met no --evidence src/tools/approvals.ts:81 --quote \"return { ok: true, approval: rec };\" --note \"Approval is only read; nothing marks it used. It can be replayed or used by parallel calls until it expires (15 minutes).\"\na check B06.4 --met no --evidence src/tools/approvals.ts:78 --quote \"if (!rec.approverRole || !policy.approval.approverRoles.includes(rec.approverRole)) {\" --note \"Approver role is checked against a global list but not against the action, and permissions and resource state (deposit, appointment) are not rechecked at execution (executor.ts:86 invokes directly).\"\na check B06.5 --met yes --evidence src/tools/approvals.ts:71 --quote 'return { ok: false, reason: `approval store unavailable: ${(err as Error).message}` };' --note \"Store error returns ok:false, so the tool is denied\" --counter \"Searched for catch blocks around checkApproval/requestApproval that continue: executor.ts:80-81 denies on !ok; requestApproval failure throws and stops the run (loop.ts:95).\"\na check B07.1 --met yes --evidence config/budgets.yaml:3 --quote \"maxTurns: 8\" --note \"Loop count, wall time, tokens, cost, tool calls, per-minute rate and peer-call cap all set (budgets.yaml:3-10)\" --counter \"Searched for unlimited values (0, -1, inf, null) and uncapped loops: for(;;) in loop.ts:55 calls budget.turn() each iteration; no unlimited settings.\"\na check B07.2 --met yes --evidence src/agent/loop.ts:56 --quote \"budget.turn();\" --note \"Harness enforces all limits via RunBudget and aborts via AbortController; executor rethrows BudgetExceeded (executor.ts:92); loop.ts:95 stops the run and hands off\" --counter \"Searched for limits settable by tool args or model output: none; limits come from config/budgets.yaml. Classifier call cost is not counted, but it is a single capped call per run.\"\na check B07.3 --met yes --evidence config/budgets.yaml:10 --quote \"this agent starts no sub-agents\" --note \"No sub-agent spawning; the peer call to the eligibility agent is counted and capped (budget.ts:154-157)\" --counter \"Searched for spawn, Task, handoff, create_agent, sub-agent: none in src.\"\na check B07.4 --met yes --evidence src/agent/budget.ts:139 --quote 'await this.shared(\"subject_daily_cost\"' --note \"Per-subject, per-tenant and fleet cost plus tenant and fleet tool-rate quotas use a shared DynamoDB conditional counter (budget.ts:32-55)\" --counter \"Searched for in-process-only counters: per-run counters are process memory but daily/rate quotas go through DynamoQuotaStore; store failures throw and stop the run.\"\na check B08.1 --met yes --evidence k8s/deployment.yaml:168 --quote \"podSelector: {}\" --note \"NetworkPolicy selects all pods, policyTypes Egress and Ingress, with egress only to DNS, the egress proxy and the EHR private-link /28\" --counter \"Searched for allow-all rules, 0.0.0.0/0, ::/0 and broad CIDRs: none.\"\na check B08.2 --met yes --evidence infra/terraform/main.tf:69 --quote \"http_put_response_hop_limit = 1\" --note \"Egress limited to proxy/DNS/EHR /28, IMDSv2 required with hop limit 1, no hostNetwork/hostPath, private EKS endpoint. Credential breadth across tenants is filed under B02.\" --counter \"Searched for 0.0.0.0/0 egress, hostNetwork true, docker.sock, hostPath: none.\"\na check B08.3 --met yes --evidence k8s/deployment.yaml:162 --quote \"kind: NetworkPolicy\" --note \"Isolation is a NetworkPolicy plus namespace Pod Security labels, not prompt or harness code\" --counter \"Searched for URL allow-lists in harness code that the model could steer: tool calls go to fixed configured hosts.\"\nEOF\n","description":"Record B01-B08 check answers"}}}
