the allowlist only blocks at call time.\" --next \"Filter registry.definitions() against the allowlist before building the tool list.\" --violates \"Enforce a role-based allowlist\"\na item B02 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"One runtime role reads every clinic's secrets and writes the approvals and control tables, and the tenant comes from model or header input.\" --next \"Take tenant only from the verified session, use per-tenant credentials, and trim IAM to the needed operations and tables.\" --violates \"Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries\"\na item B03 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"Static provider and client secrets have no rotation in the repo.\" --next \"Add Secrets Manager rotation or move to short-lived federated credentials, and document the chosen lifetimes.\" --violates \"Show that credentials expire and rotate\"\na item B04 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"No maximum revocation time is stated and the only stop path in the repo needs the agent to read a flag.\" --next \"State a revocation limit, add an enforcement-point revoke path (IAM deny, EHR client revoke), and cover open sessions.\" --violates \"Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect\"\na item B05 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Approval gate covers three tools by name only; update_appointment can cancel and eligibility check can refund without approval.\" --next \"Gate by operation, target and arguments, and route every cancel, refund and outbound send through the same gate.\" --violates \"Block them by default in the execution path\"\na item B06 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Approvals are not compared to the call's arguments or instance and are never consumed, so they can be replayed.\" --next \"Compare argsHash and agentInstanceId at execution and consume the approval with a conditional write.\" --violates \"Make approvals single-use\" --violates \"Tie each approval