{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdiHCzZ94zrkBB7ryuDQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NKSSpChEtNUDkneeSY9oFq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":". /tmp/ans_env.sh\na check R11.3 --met no --evidence src/workers/reminders.ts:27 --quote \"const unregister = killSwitch.register(ctx.runId, clinic.id, abort);\" --note \"The server watcher aborts in-flight runs within 2s (kill-switch.ts:61-75, started at server.ts:89), but the reminders job registers an AbortController and never starts the watcher, so a halt cannot abort its in-flight EHR and SMS calls; those SMS fetches have no timeout. README claims the watcher aborts in-flight requests.\"\na item R11 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"The agent's own runtime role can write the halt flag, the reminders job is never aborted mid-call, and MCP sessions stay open on stop.\" --next \"Make the control table read-only for the runtime role, start the watcher in the worker, and close MCP sessions on halt.\" --violates \"The agent's credentials must not be able to change it\" --also-affects B02 --also-affects B05\na item B09 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"The eligibility attestation's own header picks the key-set URL the agent fetches, and no redirect or resolved-IP checks exist.\" --next \"Pin the JWKS URL in config and add redirect and IP checks to outbound fetches.\" --violates \"Allow only the outside destinations the task needs\" --also-affects E07\na item R13 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Audit omits arguments, results and the policy version, and is written only after the action runs.\" --next \"Fix the policy.version field, record arguments and results, and write an intent record before the call.\" --violates \"authorization decisions with the policy version used\" --violates \"tool calls and key arguments\" --also-affects E11\na check E01.1 --met no --evidence release/manifest.json:48 --quote '\"peers\": [' --note \"Manifest lists one MCP server, one peer and three native tool groups. Not listed: identity services (group STS, chat JWKS auth), the egress proxy as a gateway entry, the DynamoDB stop channel, the Firehose audit service, Secrets Manager, and the payments and SMS providers.\"\na check E01.2 --met no --evidence release/manifest.json:44 --quote '\"owner\": \"ehr-integrations@northbay-clinics.example\"' --note \"Entries carry a single owner each, with no agent-team owner next to a platform or vendor owner; most services have none.\"\na check E01.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/payments.ts:9 --quote 'const BASE = process.env.PAYMENTS_API ?? \"https://api.payments-provider.example/v2\";' --note \"Payments API, SMS API (sms.ts:8), STS token exchange, chat JWKS and Anthropic are called by code but absent from the manifest inventory.\"\na check E02.1 --met unknown --evidence package.json:17 --quote '\"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",' --note \"Direct dependencies use exact versions and images use digests, but package-lock.json is not in the reviewed tree; the EHR MCP server is pinned only by URL and certificate (manifest.json:41-42), no version.\"\na check E02.2 --met no --evidence .github/workflows/ci.yml:20 --quote \"- run: npm ci --ignore-scripts\" --note \"No npm signature or provenance verification for packages. Cosign verification covers only the agent's own image (deploy.yml:66).\"\na check E02.3 --met no --evidence .github/workflows/ci.yml:21 --quote \"- run: npm run lint\" --note \"CI runs lint, test and build only. No npm audit, osv-scanner, trivy or grype gate; ECR scan_on_push (main.tf:92) does not gate CI.\"\na check E02.4 --met no --evidence release/manifest.json:38 --quote '\"mcpServers\": [' --note \"No dependency approval records naming publisher, permissions and update source for packages, the EHR MCP server or the peer, and no recorded exception for remote services.\"\na check E03.1 --met no --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:131 --quote 'definition: toDefinition(`${serverId}__${t.name}`, t),' --note \"Tool descriptions and schemas from the server are converted and used directly; no stored fingerprint of any approved tool exists in code, manifest or allowlist.\"\na check E03.2 --met no --evidence src/server.ts:48 --quote \"const { reportedName, meta } = await ehr.catalog();\" --note \"Catalog is loaded once at start-up and scanned only for bad content. No notifications/tools/list_changed handler and no re-check on reconnect; no fingerprint compare anywhere.\"\na check E03.3 --met no --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:126 --quote \"for (const t of scan.acceptedTools) {\" --note \"Any tool that passes the content scan is accepted; there is no approved definition to block a changed tool against.\"\na check E03.4 --met no --evidence release/manifest.json:42 --quote '\"tlsCertSha256\": \"1f6a9c3e5b7d9f1a3c5e7b9d1f3a5c7e9b1d3f5a7c9e1b3d5f7a9c1e3b5d7f9a\",' --note \"The EHR server endpoint and certificate are pinned, but no implementation version or attestation is recorded, and there is no metadata fingerprint to keep separate.\"\na prescan H011 --verdict confirmed --item E03 --reason \"ehr-mcp.ts:78 loads tools with listTools and nothing compares description or schema to an approved fingerprint; registry.ts only content-scans them.\"\na flag E03 --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:78 --note \"Tool list is fetched from the EHR MCP server and passed to the model after a content scan only; no fingerprint comparison on load, refresh or list change.\"\na check E04.1 --met yes --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:114 --quote \"scan = scanServer(meta, this.bareNamesExcept(serverId));\" --note \"scanServer covers instructions, prompts, resource templates, and per tool name, title, description, input and output schemas and annotations (metadata-scan.ts:98-130) before registration\" --counter \"Searched for other paths that load MCP metadata or pass server instructions to the model: registerMcp is the only one; server instructions are never put in the prompt.\"\na check E04.2 --met yes --evidence src/tools/metadata-scan.ts:56 --quote 'rule: \"url\"' --note \"Rules cover control and invisible characters, role overrides, markers, concealment, base64 and hex, escaped unicode, URLs, emails, phones, other-server tool names, and length limits (metadata-scan.ts:33-71)\" --counter \"Compared each required category with RULES and LIMITS: all present.\"\na check E04.3 --met yes --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:119 --quote \"if (scan.serverRejected) {\" --note \"Server-level findings reject the server and tool findings reject the tool (registry.ts:119-125)\" --counter \"Searched for log-only handling of findings: rejected entries are skipped and only logged at server.ts:53 after rejection.\"\na check E04.4 --met yes --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:116 --quote \"metadata scan error\" --note \"A throw from the scanner rejects the whole server (registry.ts:113-118); covered by controls.test.ts:86\" --counter \"Searched for flags that disable scanning or catch blocks that continue: none.\"\na check E05.1 --met yes --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:128 --quote 'key: `${serverId}__${t.name}`,' --note \"Key is the manifest-assigned serverId plus tool name; reported name is logged only (registry.ts:5-8)\" --counter \"Searched for lookups by bare name or serverInfo.name: bareNamesExcept is used only for conflict detection.\"\na check E05.2 --met yes --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:151 --quote \"if (editDistanceAtMostOne(canonical(existing.name), c)) {\" --note \"Duplicate bare names and lookalikes (homoglyphs, rn/m, edit distance one) across servers are rejected and recorded as conflicts; tests at controls.test.ts:28-44\" --counter \"Searched for silent overwrite: add() returns on conflict. Lookalikes within one server are not compared, which is one identity.\"\na check E05.3 --met yes --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:107 --quote \"const cfg = this.servers.find((s) => s.id === serverId);\" --note \"Only servers in the release manifest can contribute tools, and the allowlist names ehr__* keys, so a new server or copied name inherits nothing (controls.test.ts:14-26)\" --counter \"Searched for approval keyed by tool name or reported name: allowlist and policy use the serverId-prefixed key.\"\na check E06.1 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:36 --quote 'clinic-agent/ehr/${clinicId}' --note \"The agent connects straight to the EHR MCP endpoint (manifest.json:41) and itself holds the per-clinic client secrets from Secrets Manager; the egress policy allows the EHR /28 directly (deployment.yaml:192-195). No gateway sits between.\"\na check E06.2 --met unknown --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41 --quote 'body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),' --note \"No gateway exists. Whether the EHR server checks issuer, audience, expiry and scopes is outside this repo; the client requests a scope but no audience.\"\na check E06.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:96 --quote \"if (res.isError)\" --note \"The in-process executor authorizes by tool name, rate limits and audits, but responses are not validated (only error status is checked) and allowed calls are not audited with arguments.\"\na check E06.4 --met yes --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:116 --quote \"metadata scan error\" --note \"Scanner errors reject the server; control-table errors halt (kill-switch.ts:53); approval store errors deny (approvals.ts:71)\" --counter \"Searched for catch blocks around required checks that continue: none besides classifier, which fails to staff.\"\na check E06.5 --met unknown --evidence src/server.ts:49 --quote 'registry.registerMcp(\"ehr\", reportedName, meta, (tool, input, opts) => ehr.call(tool, input, opts));' --note \"The tool list is read once with the _catalog credential and shared by every clinic and caller, while sessions are keyed per clinic (ehr-mcp.ts:50-53). The agent is the MCP cli