ate path, and known vulnerabilities\"\na item E03 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"EHR tool descriptions and schemas are scanned once at start-up but never fingerprinted or re-checked.\" --next \"Store approved fingerprints, compare on every load and list change, and block on mismatch.\" --violates \"Take a fingerprint of each approved tool's description and schema\"\na item E04 --rating likely_pass --confidence medium --summary \"A scanner covers all metadata fields, rejects findings, and fails closed on error.\" --next \"Run recipe E04 with poisoned fixtures and the scanner off.\"\na item E05 --rating likely_pass --confidence medium --summary \"Tools are keyed by manifest server id, and duplicates and lookalikes are rejected.\" --next \"Run recipe E05 with a duplicate server.\"\na item E06 --rating gap --confidence low --summary \"The agent talks to the EHR MCP server directly with its own client secrets and responses are not validated.\" --next \"Add a gateway or document the EHR server as the enforcement point and validate responses.\" --violates \"Send MCP calls through a gateway, or a similar enforcement layer, that the agent can't get around\"\na item E07 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"The peer attestation is verified with a key set URL taken from its own header and is not bound to the request.\" --next \"Pin the peer's JWKS URL, bind attestations to request id, clinic and patient, and reject replays.\" --violates \"Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message, even validly signed ones\" --violates \"check freshness and track nonces or request IDs\" --also-affects B09\na item E08 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"Delegated eligibility checks use a patient chosen by the model, not the verified original subject.\" --next \"Check the appointment's patient against ctx.subject before delegating, and carry the subject in the exchange.\" --violates \"Authorize based on the original subject (the user or system whose authority is used) and the current actor\"\na item E09 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"A stop does not abort the reminders job mid-call, revokes no credentials, and records no completed effects for reconciliation.\" --next \"Start the watcher in the worker, close MCP sessions on stop, and record effects for reconciliation.\" --violates \"It must revoke access as needed and prevent orphaned retries or restarts\"\na item E10 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"Vendor receipts for model-driven refunds and SMS are not stored with identity and trace ids.\" --next \"Store receipt ids with the six identity fields and pass trace context to vendors.\" --violates \"Check that a vendor boundary doesn't leave any action untraceable to the agent and instance that did it\"\na item E11 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"Audit is written after the action runs and has no sequence numbers or gap alerts.\" --next \"Write the audit record before high-impact actions and add delivery receipts and alerts.\" --violates \"High-impact actions must fail closed when required audit capture isn't working\" --also-affects R13\na item E12 --rating needs_evidence --confidence low --summary \"Code cannot show a fleet incident drill or compromised-tool response.\" --next \"Run the E12 drill and record responders and the outside-reporting decision.\"\necho ok","description":"Record E01-E12 answers and fix-ups"}}}
